 "section_summary": "This section contains parts of two comprehensive statistical reports on Japanese educational institutions compiled in 1948 by the Education Unit, Research Branch of the Analysis and Research Division within SCAP's Civil Information and Education Section (CI&E). Pages 1–37 represent the concluding portion of the survey for Hokkaido Prefecture, listing municipal, town, village, private, and other ministry-operated schools (such as elementary, secondary, vocational, youth, and special schools) with enrollment and faculty statistics for April and November 1946, followed by a map of Hokkaido. Pages 38–62 comprise the introductory apparatus and comprehensive statistical tables (Parts One and Two) for Part 16 of the series covering Iwate Prefecture, summarizing educational data across administrative jurisdictions, school levels, and school types prior to the postwar 6-3-3-4 educational reorganization.",
