   "start_page": 38,
   "summary": "This report serves as Part 16 of a 47-part nationwide research study by the SCAP Civil Information and Education Section examining the structure, enrollment, and staffing of Japanese educational institutions in Iwate Prefecture prior to the postwar transition to the 6-3-3-4 system. It contains an introductory analysis explaining Japanese educational terminology, jurisdictional control categories (national, prefectural, municipal, town/village, and private), data collection methodology, and an organizational chart of the school system in 1946. Part One and Part Two present twelve detailed summary statistical tables tabulating student enrollments and full-time and part-time teachers across various school levels, types, and administrative jurisdictions as of 30 April and 30 November 1946, concluding with the title leaf for the detailed institutional roster.",
   "title": "Roster and Statistics of Japanese Educational Institutions, April and November 1946, Part 16: Iwate Prefecture (Special Report AR-302-E-A-26-16)",
